<li data-start="946" data-end="1263" class="">
<p data-start="949" data-end="971" class=""><strong data-start="949" data-end="971">Performance Gains:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="975" data-end="1263">
<li data-start="975" data-end="1128" class="">
<p data-start="977" data-end="1128" class="">The self-improving agent shows significant performance improvements, ranging from <strong data-start="1059" data-end="1073">17% to 53%</strong> on a subset of the <strong data-start="1093" data-end="1115">SWE Bench Verified</strong> benchmarks.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1132" data-end="1259" class="">
<p data-start="1134" data-end="1259" class="">Additional improvements were observed on other benchmarks, such as <strong data-start="1201" data-end="1218">LiveCodeBench</strong> and synthetically generated agent tasks.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1264" data-end="1479" class="">
<p data-start="1267" data-end="1290" class=""><strong data-start="1267" data-end="1290">Empirical Evidence:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1294" data-end="1479">
<li data-start="1294" data-end="1479" class="">
<p data-start="1296" data-end="1479" class="">The authors provide empirical evidence showing that self-referential agents can improve their implementations effectively while adhering to safety and resource efficiency constraints.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1481" data-end="1842" class="">
<p data-start="1484" data-end="1515" class=""><strong data-start="1484" data-end="1515">Open-Source Implementation:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1519" data-end="1842">
<li data-start="1519" data-end="1726" class="">
<p data-start="1521" data-end="1726" class="">The SICA framework is implemented in <strong data-start="1558" data-end="1577">standard Python</strong> (without the need for a domain-specific language). It is shared with the community to encourage further research and development of similar systems.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1730" data-end="1842" class="">
<p data-start="1732" data-end="1842" class="">The reference framework could also be used for <strong data-start="1779" data-end="1813">post-training LLMs on tool use</strong> and other <strong data-start="1824" data-end="1841">agentic tasks</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
