<li data-start="600" data-end="831" class="">
<p data-start="602" data-end="831" class="">Higher-pitched syllables or words can be associated with one font, while lower-pitched ones could be associated with another. This could simulate the feeling of "vocal variation" and allow users to see the intonation in the text.</p>
