dth:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto flex max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 text-base gap-4 md:gap-5 lg:gap-6 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden" tabindex="-1"><div class="group/conversation-turn relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="relative flex-col gap-1 md:gap-3"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="9045e017-817f-437e-9308-fe526ebe9c40" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-4o"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark"><p data-start="0" data-end="281" class="">Great. Here's a high-level <strong data-start="27" data-end="63">example of a concrete AGI module</strong>â€”focused on <em data-start="75" data-end="118">Visual Reasoning through Scene Simulation</em>â€”that includes technical structure, realistic mechanisms, and testable components. This is meant to contrast the more abstract language in the document you shared:</p>
<hr data-start="283" data-end="286" class="">
<h3 data-start="288" data-end="340" class=""><strong data-start="292" data-end="340">Module: Visual Scene Reasoning Engine (VSRE)</strong></h3>
<p data-start="342" data-end="463" class=""><strong data-start="342" data-end="354">Purpose:</strong><br data-start="354" data-end="357">
To enable AGI to reason about spatial, causal, and abstract relationships through simulated visual scenes.</p>
<hr data-start="465" data-end="468" class="">
<h4 data-start="470" data-end="488" class=""><strong data-start="475" data-end="488">1. Inputs</strong></h4>
<ul data-start="489" data-end="745">
<li data-start="489" data-end="581" class="">
<p data-start="491" data-end="581" class=""><strong data-start="491" data-end="518">Natural Language Query:</strong><br data-start="518" data-end="521">
e.g., "If I drop the glass from the table, will it break?"</p>
</li>
<li data-start="582" data-end="663" class="">
<p data-start="584" data-end="663" class=""><strong data-start="584" data-end="610">Knowledge Graph Links:</strong><br data-start="610" data-end="613">
e.g., <code data-start="621" data-end="628">glass</code> â†’ <code data-start="631" data-end="640">fragile</code>; <code data-start="642" data-end="656">table height</code> â†’ <code data-start="659" data-end="663">1m</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start="664" data-end="745" class="">
<p data-start="666" data-end="745" class=""><strong data-start="666" data-end="697">Contextual Memory Snapshot:</strong><br data-start="697" data-end="700">
