in)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto flex max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 text-base gap-4 md:gap-5 lg:gap-6 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden" tabindex="-1"><div class="group/conversation-turn relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="relative flex-col gap-1 md:gap-3"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="ad0f94f8-55a0-4621-9c44-115e6dfe9f6c" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-4o"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark"><p data-start="0" data-end="191" class="">Traditional autonomous systemsâ€”whether robots, AI agents, or self-driving vehiclesâ€”are typically built around the <strong data-start="114" data-end="133">sense-think-act</strong> architecture. Here's a breakdown of the standard modules:</p>
<hr data-start="193" data-end="196" class="">
<h3 data-start="198" data-end="236" class=""><strong data-start="202" data-end="236">1. Perception Module (Sensing)</strong></h3>
<p data-start="237" data-end="283" class=""><strong data-start="237" data-end="249">Purpose:</strong> Gather data from the environment.</p>
<ul data-start="285" data-end="454">
<li data-start="285" data-end="343" class="">
<p data-start="287" data-end="343" class=""><strong data-start="287" data-end="298">Inputs:</strong> Cameras, LiDAR, microphones, IMUs, GPS, etc.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="344" data-end="454" class="">
<p data-start="346" data-end="360" class=""><strong data-start="346" data-end="360">Functions:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="363" data-end="454">
<li data-start="363" data-end="393" class="">
<p data-start="365" data-end="393" class="">Object detection/recognition</p>
</li>
<li data-start="396" data-end="417" class="">
<p data-start="398" data-end="417" class="">Scene understanding</p>
</li>
<li data-start="420" data-end="436" class="">
<p data-start="422" data-end="436" class="">Mapping (SLAM)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="439" data-end="454" class="">
<p data-start="441" data-end="454" class="">Sensor fusion</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="456" data-end="459" class="">
<h3 data-start="461" data-end="496" class=""><strong data-start="465" data-end="496">2. Localization and Mapping</strong></h3>
<p data-start="497" data-end="576" class=""><strong data-start="497" data-end="509">Purpose:</strong> Determine where the agent is and build a model of the environment.</p>
<ul data-start="578" data-end="749">
<li data-start="578" data-end="636" class="">
<p data-start="580" data-end="636" class=""><strong data-start="580" data-end="597">Localization:</strong> e.g., Kalman filters, particle filters</p>
</li>
<li data-start="637" data-end="694" class="">
<p data-start="639" data-end="694" class=""><strong data-start="639" data-end="651">Mapping:</strong> 2D/3D maps, semantic maps, occupancy grids</p>
</li>
<li data-start="695" data-end="749" class="">
<p data-start="697" data-end="749" class=""><strong data-start="697" data-end="711">Common in:</strong> Robotics, drones, autonomous vehicles</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="751" data-end="754" class="">
<h3 data-start="756" data-end="782" class=""><strong data-start="760" data-end="782">3. Planning Module</strong></h3>
<p data-start="783" data-end="831" class=""><strong data-start="783" data-end="795">Purpose:</strong> Decide what to do and how to do it.</p>
<ul data-start="833" data-end="1079">
<li data-start="833" data-end="1003" class="">
<p data-start="835" data-end="845" class=""><strong data-start="835" data-end="845">Types:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="848" data-end="1003">
<li data-start="848" data-end="923" class="">
<p data-start="850" data-end="923" class=""><strong data-start="850" data-end="870">Motion Planning:</strong> How to move safely (pathfinding, obstacle avoidance)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="926" data-end="1003" class="">
<p data-start="928" data-end="1003" class=""><strong data-start="928" data-end="946">Task Planning:</strong> What sequence of actions to take (e.g., pick then place)</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1004" data-end="1079" class="">
<p data-start="1006" data-end="1079" class=""><strong data-start="1006" data-end="1021">Techniques:</strong> A*, RRT, symbolic planners (PDDL), reinforcement learning</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1081" data-end="1084" class="">
<h3 data-start="1086" data-end="1129" class=""><strong data-start="1090" data-end="1129">4. Decision-Making / Control Module</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1130" data-end="1180" class=""><strong data-start="1130" data-end="1142">Purpose:</strong> Convert plans into real-time actions.</p>
<ul data-start="1182" data-end="1337">
<li data-start="1182" data-end="1237" class="">
<p data-start="1184" data-end="1237" class=""><strong data-start="1184" data-end="1206">Low-level control:</strong> PID loops, trajectory tracking</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1238" data-end="1337" class="">
<p data-start="1240" data-end="1337" class=""><strong data-start="1240" data-end="1265">High-level decisions:</strong> Mode switching, behavioral logic (e.g., state machines, behavior trees)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1339" data-end="1342" class="">
<h3 data-start="1344" data-end="1380" class=""><strong data-start="1348" data-end="1380">5. Knowledge / Memory Module</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1381" data-end="1449" class=""><strong data-start="1381" data-end="1393">Purpose:</strong> Store information about the world and past experiences.</p>
<ul data-start="1451" data-end="1569">
<li data-start="1451" data-end="1569" class="">
<p data-start="1453" data-end="1463" class=""><strong data-start="1453" data-end="1463">Types:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1466" data-end="1569">
<li data-start="1466" data-end="1504" class="">
<p data-start="1468" data-end="1504" class="">World models (semantic or geometric)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1507" data-end="1524" class="">
<p data-start="1509" data-end="1524" class="">Episodic memory</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1527" data-end="1569" class="">
<p data-start="1529" data-end="1569" class="">Symbolic or sub-symbolic knowledge bases</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1571" data-end="1574" class="">
<h3 data-start="1576" data-end="1610" class=""><strong data-start="1580" data-end="1610">6. Communication Interface</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1611" data-end="1661" class=""><strong data-start="1611" data-end="1623">Purpose:</strong> Interact with humans or other agents.</p>
<ul data-start="1663" data-end="1751">
<li data-start="1663" data-end="1695" class="">
<p data-start="1665" data-end="1695" class=""><strong data-start="1665" data-end="1695">Natural Language Interface</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1696" data-end="1716" class="">
<p data-start="1698" data-end="1716" class=""><strong data-start="1698" data-end="1716">Multimodal GUI</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1717" data-end="1751" class="">
<p data-start="1719" data-end="1751" class=""><strong data-start="1719" data-end="1751">API connections or protocols</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1753" data-end="1756" class="">
<h3 data-start="1758" data-end="1814" class=""><strong data-start="1762" data-end="1814">7. Learning Module (Optional in classic systems)</strong></h3>
<p data-start="1815" data-end="1846" class=""><strong data-start="1815" data-end="1827">Purpose:</strong> Improve over time.</p>
<ul data-start="1848" data-end="1955">
<li data-start="1848" data-end="1955" class="">
<p data-start="1850" data-end="1862" class=""><strong data-start="1850" data-end="1862">Methods:</strong></p>
