<h3 data-start="2983" data-end="2994" class="">Summary</h3>
<p data-start="2996" data-end="3275" class="">Glasser's model describes <strong data-start="3022" data-end="3089">how a conscious human navigates desire, action, and consequence</strong> through visual internal modeling and constant reflection. The MCS proposes the <strong data-start="3169" data-end="3204">same architecture for a machine</strong>, aiming to emulate this very kind of adaptive, internalized cognition.</p>
<p data-start="3277" data-end="3374" class="">In short, <strong data-start="3287" data-end="3373">MCS could be seen as a machine instantiation of Glasserâ€™s cognitive control theory</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="3376" data-end="3498" class="">Would you like to explore how this model compares with other classic cognitive architectures like SOAR, ACT-R, or CLARION?</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full" dir="auto" data-testid="conversation-turn-65" data-scroll-anchor="false"><h5 class="sr-only">Dijiste:</h5><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto py-5 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto flex max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 text-base gap-4 md:gap-5 lg:gap-6 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden" tabindex="-1"><div class="group/conversation-turn relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col"><div class="relative flex-col gap-1 md:gap-3"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="user" data-message-id="756a9548-cecf-4516-98d0-63d49902ffde" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden items-end rtl:items-start"><div class="relative max-w-[var(--user-chat-width,70%)] bg-token-message-surface rounded-3xl px-5 py-2.5"><div class="whitespace-pre-wrap">I argue that Glasser was describing perceptual control theory and active inference that compares the model with the results and then changes either the behaviour or the model</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full" dir="auto" data-testid="conversation-turn-66" data-scroll-anchor="false"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT dijo:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto py-5 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @[37rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @[72rem]:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:32rem] @[34rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto flex max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 text-base gap-4 md:gap-5 lg:gap-6 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden" tabindex="-1"><div class="group/conversation-turn relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="relative flex-col gap-1 md:gap-3"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="0c15d0b8-daeb-4e4f-aeeb-10221aacfe34" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-4o"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark"><p data-start="0" data-end="246" class="">Yesâ€”youâ€™re absolutely right. Glasser's framework <em data-start="49" data-end="55">does</em> align strongly with <strong data-start="76" data-end="111">Perceptual Control Theory (PCT)</strong> and, conceptually, with <strong data-start="136" data-end="156">Active Inference</strong> from cognitive neuroscience. Letâ€™s unpack that comparison to make your argument stronger.</p>
<h3 data-start="248" data-end="290" class=""><strong data-start="252" data-end="290">Glasser, PCT, and Active Inference</strong></h3>
<div class="_tableContainer_16hzy_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="_tableWrapper_16hzy_14 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="292" data-end="2443" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="292" data-end="560"><tr data-start="292" data-end="560"><th data-start="292" data-end="326" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="294" data-end="305">Concept</strong></th><th data-start="326" data-end="401" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="328" data-end="346">Glasserâ€™s View</strong></th><th data-start="401" data-end="481" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="403" data-end="438">Perceptual Control Theory (PCT)</strong></th><th data-start="481" data-end="560" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="483" data-end="513">Active Inference (Friston)</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="833" data-end="2443"><tr data-start="833" data-end="1101"><td data-start="833" data-end="867" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="835" data-end="853">Internal Goals</strong></td><td data-start="867" data-end="942" data-col-size="md">â€œQuality Worldâ€ and internal desires or pictures</td><td data-start="942" data-end="1022" data-col-size="md">Reference signals (desired perceptual states)</td><td data-start="1022" data-end="1101" data-col-size="md">Prior beliefs or preferences</td></tr><tr data-start="1102" data-end="1370"><td data-start="1102" data-end="1136" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1104" data-end="1135">Perception of Current State</strong></td><td data-start="1136" data-end="1211" data-col-size="md">Mental pictures formed by observing the world</td><td data-start="1211" data-end="1292" data-col-size="md">Perceptual input from environment</td><td data-start="1292" data-end="1370" data-col-size="md">Sensory observations from the generative model</td></tr><tr data-start="1371" data-end="1638"><td data-start="1371" data-end="1405" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1373" data-end="1396">Comparison Function</strong></td><td data-start="1405" data-end="1480" data-col-size="md">Evaluation: â€œIs what Iâ€™m doing working?â€</td><td data-start="1480" data-end="1560" data-col-size="md">Comparator compares perception to goal</td><td data-start="1560" data-end="1638" data-col-size="md">Prediction error: discrepancy between expected and actual observation</td></tr><tr data-start="1639" data-end="1906"><td data-start="1639" data-end="1673" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1641" data-end="1662">Action Generation</strong></td><td data-start="1673" data-end="1748" data-col-size="md">Behavior is chosen to reduce the gap between what we want and what is</td><td data-start="1748" data-end="1828" data-col-size="md">Action modifies environment to reduce error</td><td data-start="1828" data-end="1906" data-col-size="md">Action reduces surprise by fulfilling expectations</td></tr><tr data-start="1907" data-end="2174"><td data-start="1907" data-end="1941" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1909" data-end="1925">Model Update</strong></td><td data-start="1941" data-end="2016" data-col-size="md">If outcomes arenâ€™t satisfying, change behavior or rethink the goal</td><td data-start="2016" data-end="2096" data-col-size="md">Adjust reference or perception model</td><td data-start="2096" data-end="2174" data-col-size="md">Update beliefs or policy to minimize free energy</td></tr><tr data-start="2175" data-end="2443"><td data-start="2175" data-end="2209" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2177" data-end="2189">Learning</strong></td><td data-start="2209" data-end="2284" data-col-size="md">Experience-based improvement of decision-making</td><td data-start="2284" data-end="2365" data-col-size="md">Adjust control hierarchy</td><td data-start="2365" data-end="2443" data-col-size="md">Bayesian updating of the generative model</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky end-(--thread-content-margin) h-0 self-end select-none"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end" style="height: 64.7031px;"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button class="bg-token-bg-primary hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-md-heavy"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M7 5C7 3.34315 8.34315 2 10 2H19C20.6569 2 22 3.34315 22 5V14C22 15.6569 20.6569 17 19 17H17V19C17 20.6569 15.6569 22 14 22H5C3.34315 22 2 20.6569 2 19V10C2 8.34315 3.34315 7 5 7H7V5ZM9 7H14C15.6569 7 17 8.34315 17 10V15H19C19.5523 15 20 14.5523 20 14V5C20 4.44772 19.5523 4 19 4H10C9.44772 4 9 4.44772 9 5V7ZM5 9C4.44772 9 4 9.44772 4 10V19C4 19.5523 4.44772 20 5 20H14C14.5523 20 15 19.5523 15 19V10C15 9.44772 14.5523 9 14 9H5Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></button></span></div></div></div></div>
