40rem] @[64rem]:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto flex max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 text-base gap-4 md:gap-5 lg:gap-6 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden" tabindex="-1"><div class="group/conversation-turn relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn"><div class="relative flex-col gap-1 md:gap-3"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="190d7291-d067-4bef-9e8d-f564586aebb6" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-4o"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark"><p data-start="0" data-end="87" class="">Thatâ€™s a powerful metaphor to bring into this comparisonâ€”and it fits surprisingly well.</p>
<p data-start="89" data-end="398" class="">In <strong data-start="92" data-end="112">1 Corinthians 12</strong>, Paul describes the <strong data-start="133" data-end="151">Body of Christ</strong> as one unified body made up of many different parts, each with a unique function, yet all essential. This metaphor can be seen as a profound <strong data-start="293" data-end="319">systems theory insight</strong>, where unity emerges from differentiated roles within a self-organizing whole.</p>
<p data-start="400" data-end="460" class="">Letâ€™s map that metaphor onto cognitive or AGI architectures:</p>
<div class="_tableContainer_16hzy_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="_tableWrapper_16hzy_14 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="462" data-end="2101" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="462" data-end="665"><tr data-start="462" data-end="665"><th data-start="462" data-end="503" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="464" data-end="490">Body of Christ Concept</strong></th><th data-start="503" data-end="594" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="505" data-end="550">PCT / Glasser / Active Inference Parallel</strong></th><th data-start="594" data-end="665" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="596" data-end="629">AGI Cognitive System Parallel</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="869" data-end="2101"><tr data-start="869" data-end="1070"><td data-start="869" data-end="909" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="871" data-end="897">Many members, one body</strong></td><td data-start="909" data-end="1000" data-col-size="md">Multiple hierarchical controllers or loops, coordinated for coherent behavior</td><td data-start="1000" data-end="1070" data-col-size="md">Modular architecture: memory, simulation, reasoning, action</td></tr><tr data-start="1071" data-end="1273"><td data-start="1071" data-end="1111" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1073" data-end="1097">Each part has a role</strong></td><td data-start="1111" data-end="1202" data-col-size="md">Each loop controls different perceptions or functions (e.g., vision vs. emotion)</td><td data-start="1202" data-end="1273" data-col-size="md">Vision module, language parser, meta-cognitionâ€”distinct yet unified</td></tr><tr data-start="1274" data-end="1476"><td data-start="1274" data-end="1314" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1276" data-end="1306">Mutual dependence of parts</strong></td><td data-start="1314" data-end="1405" data-col-size="md">Failure in one loop affects the whole system</td><td data-start="1405" data-end="1476" data-col-size="md">Failure in one module (e.g., faulty memory) breaks overall reasoning</td></tr><tr data-start="1477" data-end="1683"><td data-start="1477" data-end="1517" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1479" data-end="1508">No part is more important</strong></td><td data-start="1517" data-end="1608" data-col-size="md">All control systems are equally important to maintain harmony</td><td data-start="1608" data-end="1683" data-col-size="md">Equitable weighting of modules based on context (e.g., ethics vs. goals)</td></tr><tr data-start="1684" data-end="1889"><td data-start="1684" data-end="1724" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1686" data-end="1713">Unity through diversity</strong></td><td data-start="1724" data-end="1815" data-col-size="md">High-level purpose emerges from coordination across subsystems</td><td data-start="1815" data-end="1889" data-col-size="md">Human-like intelligence emerges from integrated multi-modal subsystems</td></tr><tr data-start="1890" data-end="2101"><td data-start="1890" data-end="1930" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1892" data-end="1914">The head is Christ</strong></td><td data-start="1930" data-end="2021" data-col-size="md">Highest-level reference frame or ultimate value system</td><td data-start="2021" data-end="2101" data-col-size="md">Could map to global goals, ethical schema, or "self-model" as top controller</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky end-(--thread-content-margin) h-0 self-end select-none"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end" style="height: 80.7031px;"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button class="bg-token-bg-primary hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-md-heavy"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M7 5C7 3.34315 8.34315 2 10 2H19C20.6569 2 22 3