<li data-start="454" data-end="637" class="">
<p data-start="456" data-end="637" class="">This reflects the core of <strong data-start="482" data-end="511">Perceptual Control Theory</strong> (PCT) and <strong data-start="522" data-end="542">Active Inference</strong>â€”where organisms maintain internal order by reducing prediction error or maintaining setpoints.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="639" data-end="691" class="">2. <strong data-start="646" data-end="691">Thermostat Maker = Evolutionary Mechanism</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="692" data-end="1042">
<li data-start="692" data-end="860" class="">
<p data-start="694" data-end="860" class="">The thermostat-maker is the <strong data-start="722" data-end="785">system or process that can construct and modify thermostats</strong>, i.e., can create regulatory architectures that adapt or change over time.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="861" data-end="1042" class="">
<p data-start="863" data-end="1042" class="">This can be interpreted as <strong data-start="890" data-end="911">natural selection</strong> or <strong data-start="915" data-end="938">a genetic algorithm</strong>â€”it builds regulators (organisms) that survive better by controlling their perceptions more effectively.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1044" data-end="1047" class="">
<h3 data-start="1049" data-end="1104" class="">What This Implies for Minimum Viable Consciousness:</h3>
